nodal (1.0.0) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Import / Export / Migration: copy-first vendor-neutral engine, Proxmox REST discovery and downloadable file-volume import, disk/OVF/libvirt/bundle adapters, No-dal portable export, compatibility ratings, and source-safety invariants. Source destruction is not a migration operation. Live and snapshot-assisted are listed as unavailable in V1. vma paths fail closed. CE is not license-gated.
  * Phase 43 CE 1.0: license-activation surface, operator docs, and API freeze. The license stub does nothing unless a key is present. An unreachable licensing API uses grace and does not stop workloads. This tree does not embed EE blobs or mint production apt signatures here. Signed install remains the documented HTTPS repo and keyring path. CE 1.0 hardware gates are not yet passed; this entry stays UNRELEASED.
  * Isolated-nat enables IPv4 forwarding from host routing state, persists it in sysctl.d, and installs per-network nftables masquerade without flushing administrator rules.
  * ndl-control relinquishes its writer lease on SIGTERM so a package upgrade or systemd restart can start immediately. Packaging no longer stops the unit on upgrade; dh_installsystemd restarts it once.
  * ndl-control maintainer scripts keep the automatic systemd helper token on its own line so debhelper cannot turn comment text into executable shell.
  * Files is a workload file manager with Monaco editing, bulk operations, and typed copy/chmod/chown. Terminal drag-and-drop uploads through the file API and inserts shell-escaped paths without executing them.
  * Terminal is a first-class workspace of independent PTY sessions. Quick Switch opens a new session against any authorized target, including one that already has tabs. Host identity stays distinct from workload shells.
  * Workloads opens a contextual operator sidebar in the same region as main navigation. Back to Main Menu restores the global sidebar without dropping Terminal workspace sessions. Hosts appear beside containers and VMs. The workload table remains on Manage.
  * Terminal fills remaining viewport space by default and can be dragged from a corner handle. The chosen size is a local workspace preference. Double-click the handle or Reset size restores fill-available behavior.
  * ndl-agent.service grants CAP_SETFCAP and CAP_SYS_PTRACE for typed lxc-attach of unprivileged system containers. NoNewPrivileges stays yes. DevicePolicy stays closed. The bounding set is not unrestricted.
  * Fail the Debian UI package unless Vite rebuilds dist during dh_auto_build. rebuild-packages.sh and the e2e builders discard any copied ui/dist so a stale frontend cannot be packed.
  * ndl-ui try-restarts ndl-control after configure. The control plane rereads index.html from disk, sends Cache-Control: no-cache for the shell, immutable caching for hashed /assets/, and 404s missing hashed files instead of SPA HTML.
  * Terminal workspace keeps each tab's xterm and PTY mounted while switching. Inactive sessions stay full-size and hidden instead of being parked in a 1px holder that resized the live shell.
  * Host Files cannot rename or follow a symlink into denied prefixes. Rename onto an existing directory fails instead of deleting that tree. Postgres data and /var/lib/ndl/secrets are denied the same way host.key already is. Restore-as-new of extra data disks is refused like clone. Migrate fails closed when a disk volume is missing. Join cert failure revokes the orphan node. Node revoke fails closed if the CA serial cannot be recorded.
  * A fenced writer cannot renew or clear the lease; mutate APIs refuse both the fenced holder and a standby until promote. Partitioned OS root marks the parent disk so ZFS/LVM/OSD create cannot wipe it. Files names reject empty and parent-directory segments before they reach the jail.
  * Overlay snapshot rollback refuses a running VM like ZFS and LVM. Template create records the new overlay as the volume tip. recover-admin fails closed when the user row is missing. MFA challenges and recovery codes are consumed before a session is issued. Migration cancel and retry fail closed when job persist fails.
  * Mutating APIs refuse a fenced writer and a standby until promote; fence and promote stay reachable. Overlay flatten refuses a running VM. Restore of a system container is refused instead of using the VM replace path.
  * System container create and clone join rootfs under the pool with HostVolumePath. An absolute or parent-directory volume locator is refused instead of path.Join discarding the pool root. System-container Files and Terminal refuse unavailable root storage the same way start does. GET no longer lists files or a 201 jail_root whose volume GET /volumes would show unavailable.
  * VM create with desired_power running fails closed when storage is unavailable instead of returning 201. Clone records desired_power running after start. System container create honors desired_power stopped. PATCH does not apply CT create to OCI workloads and fails closed when the CT agent apply fails.
  * Storage-pressure policy apply records failed migrate operations instead of leaving them queued and marking the run succeeded. Dest-agent-not-connected stays queued. Approved AI plan steps finish their task rows as succeeded or failed instead of leaving them queued.
  * Policy automation binds the seeded automation role and unbinds leftover Operator so the service identity cannot inherit tokens, feature manage, compute delete, or backups.
  * Workload delete requires compute.delete. A token scoped to compute.lifecycle can still start and stop and cannot delete.
  * Workload clone requires compute.create. PATCH of CPUs, memory, firmware, or cloud-init requires compute.modify. desired_power stays on compute.lifecycle.
  * Workloads contextual-nav test retries the main-nav click until Back to Main Menu is visible. A detached anchor can change the pathname without a popstate, which would leave Dashboard mounted.
  * Agent Files for a system container uses last-applied rootfs and fails closed when that record is missing instead of trusting client jail_root. Create and clone refuse an unclean rootfs_path before mkdir.
  * Alert webhook delivery resolves hostnames and refuses loopback, link-local, unique-local, and RFC1918 addresses. Mixed records fail closed. Delivery does not follow HTTP redirects.
  * Migration archive extract restores only user.* xattrs. security.* and trusted.* from a tar cannot land on the host.
  * OpenAPI documents the existing AAL 2 cluster.destroy, secrets.reveal, and volume unlock paths. They stay honest 422. CI fails if the HTTP mux and the freeze spec drift.
  * Approved AI plans create policies through POST /api/v1/policies instead of writing the store beside that handler.
  * nodalctl workload, network, and image upload use the same TLS client as login so a generated appliance certificate is not rejected.
  * Offline migrate dest locators join under the dest pool root. An invalid volume class cannot walk out of that pool. Relative source BackendRef is joined the same way.
  * Node GPU test waits for the IOMMU group member list. The GPUs heading renders before /gpus returns.
  * Join client TLS keeps system certificate roots and adds the cluster CA so northbound HTTPS still verifies after node.crt is written.
  * OpenAPI documents existing VM create balloon, secure_boot, and spec, OCI secret_refs and volumes, and PATCH iso_library_id and nocloud. Raw qemu_args stay undocumented and refused.
  * Migration archive extract refuses GNU sparse members instead of skipping them without error.
  * AI provider endpoints must be http(s) without userinfo so API keys stay in secrets. Completions do not follow HTTP redirects.
  * Object-store backup endpoints and OCI registry URLs must not include credentials. Access keys stay in dedicated fields and are not returned in list JSON.
  * Migration source endpoints must be http(s) without userinfo. Tokens stay in dedicated fields. An HA replica endpoint that looks like a DSN is refused so the secret stays in the DSN field.
  * Approved AI plan steps fail when the existing API handler writes no HTTP status. Create-workload steps fail when the response has no id.
  * Files copy and rename dest paths are jailed in the control plane before the agent. The Files UI refuses parent-directory dest and upload names the same way mkdir already does.
  * Migration import path and xml_path must be under No-dal storage, staging, or /tmp. OpenAPI documents the create-source token field and the start fields the handlers already use.
  * ACME directory URLs must be https without userinfo. A failed probe does not persist credentials that GET /certs would list. ACME configure fails closed if the certificate row cannot be recorded. A 200 does not list a pending or failed directory GET /certs would miss.
  * Files upload expected sha256 must match the digest field. A substring of the JSON result is not a checksum.
  * OpenAPI documents Files dest_path jail, write-only SMTP password, and HA replica host:port.
  * Backup target probe will not stat a host path outside the allowed artifact prefixes. SMB UNC locators are unchanged.
  * Files upload sha256 checksums the uploaded bytes. expected_sha256 is compare-and-swap of the existing file. They are not the same field.
  * WireGuard peer endpoint must be host:port without userinfo. Credentials stay out of listed peer JSON.
  * Backup copy dest is an allowed artifact locator such as /var/lib/ndl/backups. qemu-img convert for a VM disk still requires the storage root.
  * OpenAPI documents Directory pool backend_type routing and the library image upload fields the handlers already use.
  * NFS/SMB/iSCSI create fails closed if datastore or SMB credential persist fails. A 201 does not mean credentials were stored.
  * Distributed attach fails closed if locator or cephx persist fails. OSD create fails closed if the OSD row cannot be recorded.
  * ZFS import and create fail closed if zpool GUID identity cannot be recorded. A 201 does not skip GetZFSPoolByGUID uniqueness.
  * Cluster session listen_addr must be host:port without userinfo. Credentials stay out of listed remote node JSON. Pairing token is optional on reconnect.
  * LVM create fails closed if volume-group identity cannot be recorded. Kubelet and ceph-osd start/stop fail closed if feature runtime status cannot be recorded.
  * HA fence and promote fail closed if HA state persist fails. Replica configure already required that persist.
  * Node group create fails closed if member persist fails. A 201 does not mean node_ids were stored.
  * Viewer command palette test retries Ctrl+K until the dialog is open. The shortcut listener is attached after first paint.
  * Cluster OpenSession fails closed if the session row cannot be recorded. A 200 does not invent session_id.
  * Rolling update and policy apply fail closed if step or run persist fails. A 2xx body is not a substitute for the stored row.
  * Store install 201 fails closed if the installation row cannot be updated to succeeded. USB/PCI attach fails closed if workload spec persist fails.
  * Backup run, restore, and verify fail closed if the run or artifact verify row cannot be updated. A 202 body is not a substitute for the stored status.
  * Host update apply and rollback fail closed if the update operation row cannot be updated. Rolling update surfaces that persist error instead of inventing a step.
  * AI plan approve fails closed if plan or step persist fails. A 200 body is not a substitute for the stored plan status.
  * Workload migrate fails closed if the migrate job row cannot be created or updated. A 200 body is not a substitute for GET /migrate.
  * Service principal create, network policy apply, and VM PATCH fail closed if the catalog row cannot be recorded. A 2xx body is not a substitute for list or GET.
  * Network apply fails closed if observed status persist fails. A 200 body is not a substitute for the stored network row.
  * VM and system-container create fail closed if boot disk or NIC persist fails. Object backup target 201 fails closed if probed status cannot be recorded. Lab qemu-proto start fails closed if the disk join cannot be recorded. A 201 does not list a VM whose GET disks would miss the volume. Stop and restart fail closed if desired_power cannot be recorded. Catalog status stays the stored row; observe_status stays live.
  * OCI create and system-container clone fail closed if disk, NIC, or clone volume persist fails.
  * VM clone, library import, restore-as-new, and migration disk import fail closed if disk or NIC persist fails.
  * GPU assign and unassign fail closed if the agent apply fails or is unavailable. A 201 does not leave an assigned row the agent did not apply.
  * USB and PCI attach fail closed if the VM agent is unavailable. ApplyUSB failure restores spec like ApplyVFIO. A 201 does not claim a device the agent did not apply.
  * System-container PATCH fails closed if the workload agent is unavailable. A 200 does not rewrite CPUs or desired_power the host did not apply.
  * Store install GPU assign fails closed if the agent apply fails or is unavailable. A 201 does not leave an assigned row the agent did not apply.
  * Files chmod applies mode 0. Omitted mode is still required; mkdir still defaults 0755.
  * Restore-replace refuses extra data disks like restore-as-new. Boot replace does not mix with unrestored data volumes. Migration bundle export refuses extra data disks the same way. Offline and live migrate refuse extra data disks the same way. Dest incoming compiles one boot disk. GET no longer claims dest ownership of unrestored data volumes. Backup of extra data disks is refused before a run or artifact is recorded. A 202 does not create a boot-only copy restore cannot apply. Nightly policy ticks skip that VM instead of storing a succeeded boot-only run. VM import from the library refuses ISO items. Create already refuses a cloud-image as installation media. CopyBackup would qemu-img that ISO as qcow2. GET no longer lists a VM whose boot disk is that ISO.
  * Node maintain records succeeded or failed after a local dest migrate instead of leaving the listed operation queued. Extra-disk migrate 422 is visible on GET /tasks.
  * PCI attach applies the union of VFIO hosts already assigned to the VM. A second passthrough does not drop the first from frozen argv. GPU VFIO assign merges and unassign subtracts instead of wiping every host.
  * GPU VFIO assign records pci_hosts on the VM spec so start reprepare cannot drop the bound devices. Unassign removes those hosts from spec.
  * Template create refuses extra data disks like clone. Clone and template refuse catalog extra data disks the same way spec extra disks already are. A 201 does not copy only the boot volume. Deploy clones the live source, so a boot-only overlay must not be recorded as a usable template.
  * USB attach on a running VM fails closed if live QMP device_add fails. A stopped VM still records usb-host in frozen argv without inventing a live hotplug. The southbound client treats Execute Ok false as an apply error.
  * VM delete releases USB and exclusive GPU/PCI claims before runtime is removed. PCI unassign restores the assignment BDF when pci_devices is empty.
  * Logout fails closed if the session row cannot be revoked. A 204 does not clear a cookie while the session remains valid.
  * Store install fails closed if the stack member cannot record the created workload. A 201 does not leave GET /stacks with a null member workload_id.
  * Node maintain fails closed if a queued migrate operation cannot be recorded. A 200 does not invent migrate_operation_id.
  * Storage-pressure policy apply fails closed if a queued migrate operation cannot be recorded. A 200 does not invent operation_ids that GET /tasks would miss.
  * AI plan approve stops if the task row cannot be recorded. A succeeded plan does not invent operation_id that GET /tasks would miss.
  * Overlay snapshot after flatten does not inherit leftover catalog parent_id. Flattened depth is a new chain.
  * Template snapshot catalog records the frozen overlay backing, not the live -tmpl.qcow2 tip. Rollback overlays that frozen parent. Deploy still clones the live source.
  * Cluster OpenSession fails closed if a pairing token cannot be marked used. A 200 does not leave the token reusable.
  * Host update apply and rollback fail closed if the update operation row cannot be created. A 200 does not invent an operation id that GET /updates would miss.
  * Backup overlay after flatten does not inherit leftover catalog parent_id. Flattened depth is a new chain.
  * Template overlay honors the qcow2 chain cap and records catalog parent_id and chain_depth like user and backup overlays. Flattened depth is a new chain.
  * Overlay snapshot after rollback does not inherit leftover catalog parent_id. Rolled-back depth is a new chain.
  * MFA confirm fails closed if the method cannot be marked enabled. A 200 does not invent enabled that GET /mfa would miss.
  * Second template overlay uses a unique -tmpl.qcow2 tip so overlay path is not the live backing. qemu-img create refuses dest equal to backing.
  * Live migrate 200 workload JSON is re-read after observed persist. A
    200 does not invent dest running or reason that GET /workloads would
    miss.
  * Network policy apply loads every stored policy in one nft table
    replace. Applying one policy does not drop sibling rules while GET
    still shows them available.
  * DELETE of a missing migration source fails closed. Postgres no longer
    returns 200 ok when no catalog row was removed.
  * Network apply, backup verify, live migrate job, import/export job, and
    rolling plan persist fail closed on Postgres UPDATE of zero rows. A 2xx
    does not invent status GET would miss.
  * Group member add fails closed for a missing user and is idempotent. A
    200 does not invent membership GET /groups would miss, and a second add
    does not 404.
  * Node group create fails closed for a missing node_id. Memory no longer
    invents membership GET /node-groups would list for a node GET would
    miss.
  * VM PATCH iso_library_id fails closed when the library item is missing
    or is not installation media. A 200 does not invent an ISO GET
    /images would miss. Empty iso_library_id still detaches.
  * Network policy create fails closed for an empty or missing workload id.
    An empty src_workload_id no longer borrows another VM MAC. A missing
    workload is 404, and GET /networks does not list a policy.
  * Overlay chain depth counts a live qcow2 overlay that snapshot catalog
    persist missed, including that file when a later snapshot stores it as
    BackendRef. A follow-on 201 cannot exceed the chain cap of 16. Flatten
    and rollback tips still start a new chain.
  * AI plan approve fails closed when plan status persist writes zero rows
    or the stored status does not match. A 200 does not invent executing
    or succeeded that GET /ai/plans would still show as preview.
  * Overlay create refuses VNI 0 before persist. fakeNet and an unavailable
    agent no longer 201 a catalog row GET /networks would list that apply
    cannot install.
  * Bond create refuses empty members, invalid member ifnames, and modes
    other than active-backup or 802.3ad before persist. fakeNet and an
    unavailable agent no longer 201 a catalog row GET /networks would list
    that apply cannot install.
  * VLAN create refuses a missing or invalid parent ifname, modes other
    than access or trunk, and an invalid access ifname before persist.
    fakeNet and an unavailable agent no longer 201 a catalog row GET
    /networks would list that apply cannot install.
  * WireGuard peer create refuses a listen port outside 1-65535 and
    addresses that are not CIDR before persist. fakeNet no longer 201 a
    catalog row GET /cluster/wg would list that apply cannot install.
  * Network policy create refuses an action apply cannot install and a
    source that is the destination before persist. GET /networks no
    longer lists a policy apply cannot install.
  * DHCP reservation create refuses an address outside the isolated
    subnet or equal to the gateway or network address before persist.
    GET /networks/{id}/reservations no longer lists a mapping apply
    cannot install.
  * Terminal session create refuses a cwd that escapes the jail, matching
    Files. GET /io/sessions no longer lists a session whose connect path
    would silently start at the jail root.
  * HA replica endpoint must be host:port. A DSN without userinfo is no
    longer stored as replica_endpoint that GET /cluster/ha would list.
    Credentials stay in the dsn field.
  * Distributed OSD create fails closed when pool_id is missing. A 201
    does not invent a pool_id GET /storage/pools would miss. Empty
    pool_id is still optional.
  * Store install GPU assign refuses a PCI address that is not in node
    inventory before persist, matching POST /gpus/assign. fakeGPU no
    longer 201 an assignment GET /workloads/{id}/gpus would list that
    GET /gpus would miss.
  * Network create and apply refuse a LAN-bridge without a valid uplink
    ifname and an isolated ipv4_cidr BuildPlan cannot install before
    persist. fakeNet no longer 201 a catalog row GET /networks would
    list that apply cannot install. Empty isolated CIDR still defaults
    to 10.64.0.0/24.
  * Backup NFS and SMB create refuse a relative locator that is not
    server:/export or //server/share, and refuse parent-directory
    segments, before persist. SMB UNC is not passed through the Unix
    artifact jail. GET /backups/targets no longer lists garbage that
    apply cannot use. Absolute artifact paths stay AllowedArtifactPath.
  * VM create refuses an extra NIC network_id GET /networks would miss
    before persist. NIC rows and launch bridges follow each spec NIC
    network, so GET spec.nics cannot claim a network the TAP is not on.
  * ZFS and LVM volume create refuse an unsupported class before persist.
    fakeZFS and fakeLVM no longer 201 a catalog row GET /volumes would
    list that apply cannot create. Directory still stores the agent handle
    class.
  * Volume create refuses a size apply cannot allocate before persist.
    Block and LVM volumes require 1 MiB. Directory, ZFS zvol, LVM, iSCSI,
    and distributed no longer 201 a catalog row GET /volumes would list
    that qemu-img, zvol, thin LV, or RBD cannot create. ZFS datasets are
    not given a block minimum.
  * VM create refuses a boot disk smaller than the volume engine floor
    before persist. fakeStorage no longer 201 a workload whose GET volume
    size_bytes qemu-img cannot allocate.
  * Directory template volume create and lab qemu-proto refuse a block
    size below 1 MiB before persist. GET /volumes no longer lists a
    qcow2 apply cannot allocate.
  * Workload NIC list is ordered by created_at then id, matching
    Postgres. GET /workloads nics no longer shuffles extra NIC
    network_id under Memory map iteration.
  * Workload disk list is ordered by slot, created_at, then id,
    matching Postgres. GET /workloads disks no longer shuffles extra
    data disks under Memory map iteration.
  * GET /networks vlan, bond, policy, and overlay lists, and GET
    reservations, are ordered by created_at then id, matching
    Postgres. Nested catalog arrays no longer shuffle under Memory
    map iteration.
  * GET /workloads, /networks items, /storage/pools, /storage/volumes,
    and /storage/images are ordered by created_at then id, matching
    Postgres. Collection lists no longer shuffle under Memory map
    iteration.
  * GET /node-groups is ordered by name then id. GET WireGuard peers,
    remote nodes, distributed OSDs, migration sources, and service
    principals are ordered by created_at then id, matching Postgres.
    GET /migration/jobs and GET /workloads/{id}/migrate return newest
    jobs first, matching Postgres created_at DESC, so a later job is
    not hidden behind map iteration. Workload migrate GET looks up
    that workload's latest job instead of scanning a 50-row cluster
    window that can hide it. Host update rollback looks up the latest
    check version the same way instead of scanning a 20-row cluster
    window that can hide it.
  * VM create refuses an extra data disk whose storage pool is
    unavailable before persist. GET /workloads no longer lists a VM
    whose extra volume start cannot attach.
  * OCI create refuses an unavailable volume, storage pool, or
    network before persist. GET /workloads no longer lists a
    container whose mount or NIC apply cannot attach. OCI start
    and PATCH refuse an unavailable volume, pool, or network
    before the agent start, matching system-container start.
    GET no longer claims desired_power running when start cannot
    mount or attach.
  * VM create and PATCH refuse installation media that is not
    available, matching cloud-image create. GET spec.iso_library_id
    no longer claims an ISO GET /images would show unavailable.
  * VM create and PATCH refuse ISO or cloud-image library items whose
    storage pool is unavailable before persist. GET spec no longer
    claims media start or convert cannot read.
  * System-container create with an existing volume_id refuses a
    non-container-root class and an unavailable volume or pool, and
    joins rootfs under that volume's pool. GET /workloads no longer
    lists a container whose root apply cannot mount.
  * VM create with an existing boot volume_id refuses an unavailable
    boot pool before persist. GET /workloads no longer lists a VM
    whose boot disk start cannot attach.
  * System-container clone refuses an unavailable source volume or
    pool before persist. GET /workloads no longer lists a clone
    whose root apply cannot copy, and no clone volume is stored.
  * VM import refuses an unavailable library item, library pool,
    dest pool, or network before persist. GET /workloads no longer
    lists an import copy or start cannot apply, and no dest volume
    is stored.
  * VM clone, export, snapshot, template, backup, restore, and
    migrate refuse an unavailable boot volume or pool before persist.
    GET no longer lists a clone, library export, or overlay whose
    copy or snapshot apply cannot use the boot disk.
  * Migration disk import refuses an unavailable dest pool or
    network before persist. GET /workloads no longer lists an
    import copy or start cannot apply, and no dest volume is stored.
  * Volume create, library upload, stack named-volume import, and
    distributed RBD create refuse a failed storage pool, matching
    available-or-warning. GET no longer lists a volume, image, or
    stack whose apply cannot allocate.
  * VLAN create refuses an unavailable parent network before apply.
    GET /networks no longer lists a VLAN whose parent bridge apply
    cannot attach.
  * Lab qemu-proto start refuses an unavailable existing volume
    before persist. GET /lab/qemu-proto no longer claims a disk
    start cannot attach.
  * System-container start refuses an unavailable root volume, pool,
    or network before the agent start. GET no longer claims
    desired_power running when start cannot mount or attach.
  * System-container PATCH refuses an unavailable root volume, pool,
    or network, and an invalid volume locator, before persist. GET
    no longer claims CPUs the host apply cannot jail.
  * VM start and clone reprepare refuse an unavailable ISO library
    item before attach. GET no longer claims desired_power running
    when start cannot attach media GET /images would show unavailable.
  * VM import, migration disk import, and orphan restore refuse an
    unavailable fallback dest pool before persist. Omitting pool_id
    no longer 201s onto a failed first pool GET would list.
	* Lab qemu-proto start joins an existing volume with HostVolumePath.
    A ZFS zvol is the device path start attaches, not a path under
    the pool root JoinUnder would invent. Disk format follows
    QEMUFormat, so a zvol, thin LV, RBD, or iSCSI LUN starts as raw the
    same way product VM start already does. GET disk_format is not a
    catalog zvol or rbd string compile refuses. An existing
    container-root is refused the same way VM boot is not a
    filesystem volume. GET /lab/qemu-proto no longer claims a
    directory mount start would attach as a disk.
  * Files and Terminal join a system-container root with HostVolumePath.
    A ZFS dataset under the ZFS mount root is that path, not a nested
    JoinUnder of the absolute locator.
  * VM create on a distributed pool allocates an RBD handle and attaches
    that device. Compile accepts RBD, NBD, thin LV, and iSCSI locators the
    same way qemu-img already does. A directory qcow2 is not stored under
    /dev/rbd. Clone, export, import, restore, and qemu-proto new disks
    refuse device-backed pool roots. System-container create on RBD or
    iSCSI is 422 like clone.
  * CompileLaunch accepts mapped RBD, thin LV, NBD, and iSCSI boot disks
    the same way ValidateDiskPath already does. A frozen Launch for a
    distributed VM is argv the host can start, not a disk path refuse.
    Generic /dev remains refused. Runtime cidata and firmware locators
    still compile under the per-VM runtime prefix.
  * Library image upload refuses a distributed RBD or iSCSI pool before
    persist. GET /images no longer lists an ISO under /dev/rbd that
    Compile cannot attach.
  * Stack import and Store install refuse named Directory volumes on a
    distributed RBD or iSCSI pool before persist. GET no longer lists a
    stack whose compose volumes are directory files under /dev/rbd.
  * OCI create refuses a vm-disk bind the same way system-container create
    refuses a non container-root. GET no longer lists an application
    container whose volume apply would bind a qcow2 or RBD device.
  * VM clone, export, import, restore, and migration disk import refuse a
    ZFS or LVM-thin dest the same way they refuse RBD and iSCSI. qemu-img
    convert does not write a directory qcow2 onto a zvol or thin LV.
    Restore-replace of a qcow2 artifact onto a zvol, thin LV, RBD, or
    iSCSI LUN is refused before stop or copy. BackupReplace dest format
    is qcow2 and those volumes start as raw. Migration bundle export
    refuses a zvol, thin LV, RBD, or iSCSI source before the job is
    recorded. ConvertImport would treat that raw device as qcow2.
    Template overlay is refused; ZFS and LVM snapshots stay native.
    Snapshot, template, flatten, and backup of a mapped RBD or iSCSI LUN
    are refused before persist. GET no longer lists a qcow2 overlay or
    backup run those backends cannot create. GET no longer lists a clone
    whose start would attach a qcow2 as raw. Offline migrate refuses
    that zvol copy before ownership moves. Offline migrate also refuses
    a missing source pool and an unavailable dest directory pool before
    the job is recorded. GET no longer claims dest ownership copy cannot
    write.

